      {
        "id": 61911,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-09T18:13:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Gislef\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gislef:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It's an \"in case of emergency\" reactive power.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's true, but is also gives him an ability that his deck didn't have. if you were making a team, and wanted to include Ongoing destruction, you wouldn't need a new character.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Gislef\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gislef:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We also typically play random-selection.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This, as you saw, could actually be a problem with B:EoW. There are several villains that don't have Ongoings, and his ability won't have any effect.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Gislef\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gislef:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The power he needs to get through his deck faster to get the Modes (Initialize) is the power he loses.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p> Actually, Initialize doesn't give Bunker an extra card, it gives Bunker an extra play. He can still draw 2 cards a turn. Whether or not it is worth playing a card and drawing one or drawing 2 is something you need to decide.  </p>\n<p> Also, if you are specifically bringing a hero to destroy Ongoings (like against IL), B:EoW actaully has one of the highest chances of getting the right cards sooner, since there are 9 in his deck. </p>\n<p> Anyhoo, on to the next game. </p>",
